    "synthesis": "# Adversarial Audit Synthesis — `corpus/index/` (27 entries)\n\n**Scope of confidence.** 12 of 27 entries received a full adversarial pass (288 filed defects); of those, 93 findings were put through independent verification — 89 CONFIRMED (several with severity or mechanism corrected), 4 REFUTED. The remaining 15 entries were censused mechanically corpus-wide (parse, count, header, ID, git, ingest, runtime-reach) but not read line-by-line. Every number below was recomputed by me against the filesystem; where a prior number survived, I say so.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Corrected census\n\n`corpus/index/` holds **1,759 files / 34.63 MB** across 27 entry directories (`.backups/` excluded; it holds a further 6.42 MB). By extension: **865 .md, 494 .json, 219 edge-CSVs, 67 .mmd, 25 .svg**.\n\n| # | Entry | Layout family | Reg? | Units | Analyses | Per-src edges | Synth edges | .mmd | Runtime nodes | Defects |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | A Grammar of Motives (Burke 1945) | monograph units+`_synthesis` | Y hdr | 14 (28 files) | 14 | 878 | 876 (+878 pre-canon) | 5 | 55 | 23 |\n| 2 | A Rhetoric of Motives (Burke 1950) | monograph units+`_synthesis` | Y hdr | 8 | 8 | 420 | 420 | 1 | 38 | 18 |\n| 3 | Aristotelian Emotion Secondary (1975-2015) | article-per-folder cluster | **N** | 5 | 5 | 210 | 210 | 0 | **0** | – |\n| 4 | Aristotelian Motion and Time Secondary | cluster (1-unit stub) | **N** | 1 | 1 | 58 | 0 | 0 | **0** | – |\n| 5 | Aristotelian Phantasia Secondary (1985-2017) | article-per-folder cluster | **N** | 8 | 8 | 708 | 706 | 5 | **0** | – |\n| 6 | Aristotle - Complete Works | flat work-mapped | Y tbl | 34 | 34 | 246 | 156 | 8 | 162¹ | 29 |\n| 7 | Boredom Experiment (VR Attention Study) | md-only Part III lite | Y hdr | 0 | 5 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 7 | – |\n| 8 | Boredom Secondary (Part III) | article-per-folder cluster | Y hdr | 55 | 55 | 1,918 | 1,897 | 5 | 61 | 33 |\n| 9 | Dissertation | pipeline run-history | **N** | 7 sections ×2 runs (45 files) | 55 | 1,682 (841 distinct) | 0 | 0 | **0** | 28 |\n| 10 | Game-Behavior Analysis Method (Burke × Calleja) | flat method-workshop | **N** | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **0** | 19 |\n| 11 | Heidegger - BCAP | structured/analysis pair | Y tbl | 13 | 13 | 0 | 93 | 4 | 20 | – |\n| 12 | Heidegger - Being and Time | structured/analysis pair | Y hdr | 17 | 17 | 0 (299 in fenced JSON) | 284 | 5 | 32 | 22 |\n| 13 | Heidegger - FCM | units+`_synthesis` | Y hdr | 15 | 15 | 428 | **452** | 0 | 28 | – |\n| 14 | Heidegger and Rhetoric | article-per-folder | Y hdr | 8 (16 files) | 8 | 0 | 204 | 5 | 30 | – |\n| 15 | In-Game (Calleja 2011) | monograph units+`_synthesis` | Y hdr | 13 (26 files) | 13 | 736 | 736 (+736 pre-canon) | 5 | 44 | 23 |\n| 16 | Presence Theory (Foundations) | md-only Part III lite | Y hdr | 0 | 4 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 10 | – |\n| 17 | RDR2 (Salvo Playthrough) | flat data/video | **N** | 0 | 22 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **0** | 33 |\n| 18 | RDR2 Secondary (2019-2023) | article-per-folder cluster | **N** | 12 | 12 | 506 | 506 | 5 | **0** | – |\n| 19 | Rhetoric of Interactivity and VR (Part III) | md-only Part III lite | Y hdr | 0 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 7 | – |\n| 20 | Rickert - Ambient Rhetoric | structured/analysis pair | Y hdr | 10 | 10 | 0 | 56 | 3 | 24 | – |\n| 21 | Social Presence in Virtual Worlds (Part III) | md-only Part III lite | Y hdr | 0 | 3 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 10 | – |\n| 22 | Uncomfortable Situations | monograph units+`_synthesis` | Y hdr | 6 | 6 | 373 | 371 | 5 | 36 | 21 |\n| 23 | VR Pedagogy Secondary (Part III) | article-per-folder cluster | Y hdr | 34 | 34 | 1,131 | 1,129 | 5 | 60 | 36 |\n| 24 | Veri(dis)similitude (Salvo MA) | md-only flat | **N** | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **0** | 23 |\n| 25 | Virtual Learning Environments (King–Salvo) | md-only Part III lite | Y hdr | 0 | 6 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 18 | – |\n| 26 | Von Uexkull - A Foray… | structured/analysis pair | Y hdr | 14 | 14 | 0 | 152 | 5 | 35 | – |\n| 27 | Wendt - Design for Dasein | units+`_synthesis` | Y hdr | 8 | 8 | 307 | 307 | 0 | 15 | – |\n\n¹ Aristotle's 162 are spread over 10 label strings (`Aristotle - Complete Works` 26, `- Rhetoric` 18, `- Metaphysics` 12, `- De Anima` 11, `- Physics` 11, `- Sense and Sensibilia` 11, `- On Things Heard` 9, `- On Colours` 8, `- On Memory` 8, `- Movement of Animals` 6, plus merged multi-text nodes) — an artifact of `ARISTOTLE_WORK_MAP` at `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:135+`, not of the entry.\n\n### Corrected totals, with derivation\n\n**Analytical units: 320 with a structured record, 362 addressable.**\nSum of the Units column above = 320 distinct units carrying a JSON record. Adding the 42 md-only units with an analysis but no record (Boredom Experiment 5, Presence Theory 4, RDR2 Playthrough 22, Rhetoric of Interactivity 2, Social Presence 3, VLE 6) gives **362 addressable units**. The *file* count of unit records is 355, because Grammar, In-Game and Heidegger and Rhetoric each ship a Phase-1 metadata JSON *and* a Phase-2 deep JSON per unit.\n\n> **Prior audit \"~310 unit records\" is low by 10 (distinct units) or by 45 (record files).** The gap is Grammar/In-Game/H&R double-serialization plus the 15 entries never itemized.\n\n**Unit analyses: 372.**\nSum of the Analyses column. Corpus-wide there are 865 `.md` files; only 372 are per-unit analyses. The remainder are synthesis deliverables, manuals, concordances, overviews, run-history and 96 RDR2 frame logs.\n\n> **Prior audit \"691 unit analyses\" is wrong by +319 — it is inflated by ~86%.** The likely cause is counting every `.md` inside an entry: Dissertation contributes 273 `.md` but only 55 unit analyses; RDR2 Playthrough contributes 96 `.md` but 22 beat-maps.\n\n**Distinct edge rows on disk: 9,702.**\nDerivation, per entry, taking the larger of the two layers where one is a projection of the other and the union where they are disjoint:\nGrammar 878 + RM 420 + AES 210 + AMT 58 + Phantasia 708 + **Aristotle 368 (union — see below)** + Boredom Sec 1,918 + Dissertation 841 + **FCM 450 (synthesis is a superset)** + H&R 204 + In-Game 736 + RDR2 Sec 506 + Uncomfortable 373 + VR Ped 1,131 + Wendt 307 + BCAP 93 + BT 293 + Rickert 56 + Uexkull 152 = **9,702**.\n\n> **Prior audit \"~9,762 distinct edges\" is within 0.6% — effectively CONFIRMED**, though the composition differs. Note that **19,770 rows are serialized on disk across 219 edge-CSVs** — roughly 2.04× the distinct count, because of dual-layer serialization, two `global-edges-pre-canonical.csv` files, and Dissertation's byte-identical second run.\n\n**Layer-relationship corrections (this refutes the prior audit's framing outright):**\nThe prior claim that per-source and synthesis CSVs are \"the SAME data serialized twice, but four entries disagree… nothing records which is stale\" is wrong in three different ways, and the four cited discrepancies have four *different* causes:\n\n| Entry | per / synth | Actual relationship |\n|---|---|---|\n| Boredom Secondary | 1,918 / 1,897 | Synthesis is a **lossy projection**: distinct `(source,relation,target)` = 1,897 exactly. 21 rows lost their `locus`+`note`. Disclosed at `corpus/index/Boredom Secondary (Part III)/_synthesis/cluster-ontology.md:133`. |\n| VR Pedagogy | 1,131 / 1,129 | **Ad-hoc removal of exactly 2 rows** mislabelled \"dedup\" at `_synthesis/cluster-ontology.md:161` — no key-based pass ran (5 duplicate keys / 7 surplus rows survive in the synthesis layer). Plus 12 notes destroyed by comma-truncation, e.g. `_synthesis/global-edges.csv:625`. |\n| **FCM** | 428 / **452** | Synthesis is a **strict SUPERSET** (426 ⊂ 450 distinct). 24 edges were authored only at synthesis level. Not staleness at all — the opposite direction from what was claimed. |\n| Aristotle | 246 / 156 | **Near-disjoint.** Only 33 of 368 distinct triples shared; per-source uses Greek-script node ids, `global-edges.csv` uses latin snake_case. An abandoned partial re-encoding. |\n| Grammar | 878 / 876 | 2 exact duplicate triples merged, **documented** at `_synthesis/canonical-id-resolution-report.md:33-37`. Consistent. |\n| Phantasia | 708 / 706 | 2 rows, same class as VR Pedagogy. |\n| A Rhetoric of Motives | 420 / 420 | Same count, **24 rows differ** by an undocumented space→hyphen ID normalisation. |\n\n**Runtime reach: the single most important number.** `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py` opens **48 of 1,759 files** — 903,622 of 34,626,593 bytes = **2.61%** — and parses substantially less than that (only §3A of each ontology). It contains **zero occurrences of the string `csv`** and **zero of `mmd`**. Output: 701 `ontologyNodes`, 72 `crossPipelineHooks` (100% Aristotle, hardcoded at `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:1239-1244`), 64 `tensionEdges`, 1,722 `canonicalTerms`.\n\nSo: **9,702 authored edges reach runtime = 0. 3,597 claim-shaped records reach runtime = 0. 1,623 mermaid arrows reach runtime = 0.**\n\n---\n\n## 2. The schema census\n\nThis is the input to a normalization layer. All figures recomputed.\n\n### 2.1 Unit-JSON shape families — **146 distinct top-level key signatures**\n\nNamed families, by population:\n\n| Family | Signature (top-level keys) | Entries | n |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Cluster-16** | `bridges, citation, concepts, constructs, depth, discipline, extraction, id, interlocutors, measures, readings, sections, slug, strand, tensions, thesis` | Boredom Secondary | 49 |\n| **Aristotle-Manifest-15** | `bekker_range, books, cluster, dissertation_critical, greek_terms_expected, label, latin_title, pdf_file, pdf_pages, tags, tier, two_pass, unit_id, work, work_title` | Aristotle | 34 |\n| **Cluster-16-conditions** | Cluster-16 with `conditions` replacing `measures` | VR Pedagogy | 24 |\n| **Segment-7** | `chapter, division, label, note, part, sections, unit_id` | Being and Time | 17 |\n| **Segment-6** | `chapters, dissertation_critical, label, part, two_pass, unit_id` | Von Uexkull | 14 |\n| **Segment-8** | `chapter, note, pages, part, pdf_pages, sections, title, unit_id` | BCAP | 13 |\n| **Cluster-15-game** | adds `game_elements, debate_axis_positions, themes, cluster_citations` | RDR2 Secondary | 11 |\n| **GM-Phase1-23** | `body_page_count … triple_pass_flag, unit_id` (planning stub, `expected_*` fields) | Grammar | 10 |\n| **Segment-8-chapterid** | `chapter_id, chapter_number, note, pages, part, pdf_pages, sections, title` | Rickert | 9 |\n| **RM-Deep-12** | `book_pp, calleja_pim_candidates, concepts, edge_count, heading, interlocutors, outline, pdf_pp, pentad_term_tags, positions, tensions, unit_id` | Rhetoric of Motives | 5 |\n| **FCM-Deep-19 / FCM-Deep-11** | `anchor_phrases, book_pp, bridge_relevance, claims, …` (two variants) | FCM | 4 + 4 |\n| **Article-20/21** | `abstract_paraphrase, aristotle_loci, author, … venue, year` | AES, AMT, Phantasia | ~14 |\n| **Diss-Claim-*** | 6 mutually incompatible shapes in ONE run (`_compactness_note/claim_id_format/…` vs `quality_gates/…` vs `claim_count_actual/…`) | Dissertation | 12 |\n| **GM/IG-Deep-singletons** | 18 one-off signatures of 16–28 keys; no two Grammar deep records share a shape | Grammar, In-Game | 18 |\n\nSub-schema drift is worse than top-level drift. In Boredom Secondary the `readings` array alone takes **8 incompatible object shapes** across 52 populated units: `(claim,locus,stance,tag,type)`×257, `(id,locus,text)`×167, `(loci,summary,target_fcm_unit)`×12, `(claim,page,provenance)`×8, `(claim,locus,stance,type)`×7, `(loci,summary,tag,target_fcm_unit)`×5, `(claim,loci,stance,target)`×4, `(locus,relation,summary,target)`×3. Three interchangeable locus keys corpus-wide: `locus` / `loci` / `page` / `book_page` / `pdf_page` / `anchor`.\n\n### 2.2 Edge-CSV header dialects — **44 distinct** (prior audit: 42; the extra 2 are CRLF variants that collapse under `head -1 | sort -u`)\n\nDominant dialects:\n\n| Files | Header | Entries |\n|---|---|---|\n| 107 | `source,relation,target,locus,note` | Boredom Sec, RDR2 Sec, VR Pedagogy, Wendt |\n| 16 | `source,relation,target,locus,provenance,note` | FCM |\n| 12 | `source_id,relation,target_id,domain,centrality_tier,book_page,provenance,notes` | Grammar, In-Game |\n| 12 | `source_claim,relation,edge_domain,target,note,location` | Dissertation |\n| 9 | `source,relation,target,domain,provenance,book_page` | A Rhetoric of Motives |\n| 9 | `source,target,relation,domain,weight,units,evidence` | Aristotle |\n| 8 | `source_id,relation,target_id,domain,evidence_pdf_page,evidence_bekker_or_page,contributor,notes` | Phantasia |\n| 6 | `source,relation,target,domain,evidence,contributor` | AES |\n| 3 | as row 1 but **CRLF** | Boredom Sec (bor-sec-10, -14, -48) |\n| 1 each ×31 | see below | – |\n\nThe 31 singleton dialects are concentrated: **Grammar contributes 12** (`src,rel,dst,book_page,note`; `edge_id,source,source_type,relation,target,target_type,evidence_page,provenance,notes`; `source_id,source_type,relation,target_id,target_type,book_p,provenance,notes`; …), **In-Game 8**, **Uncomfortable Situations 5**. Column counts range 5–12. Single-entry outliers: Aristotelian Motion and Time (`edge_id,contributor,source_type,source_id,relation,target_type,target_id,target_label,evidence_locus,strength,note`), BCAP (`source,relation,target,edge_domain,note,units`), BT (`source,target,relation,edge_domain,units,note` — same six names as BCAP, **different order**), H&R, Rickert, Uexkull.\n\n**Filename dialects matter too.** A `*-edges.csv` glob misses: all 8 A Rhetoric of Motives per-unit files (named plain `edges.csv`, and their basenames are non-unique across the tree), and `_synthesis/global-edges-pre-canonical.csv` in Grammar and In-Game.\n\n### 2.3 Relation vocabulary — **633 distinct values over 19,770 rows** (prior audit: 633 — CONFIRMED exactly)\n\nTop-20: `cites` 2,986 · `defines` 1,827 · `treats-construct` 1,000 · `instances-in-text` 928 · `extends` 666 · `qualifies` 570 · `contests` 547 · `cites-as-support` 534 · `grounds` 452 · `bridges-to-part-iii` 397 · `depends_on` 382 · `bridges-to-pipeline` 343 · `cites-cluster-author` 322 · `treats-game-element` 288 · `shifts-debate-axis` 260 · `instantiates` 217 · `operationalizes-measure` 207 · `exemplifies` 198 · `refines` 196 · `operationalizes` 193.\n\nDistinct relations **per entry** — this is where the sprawl lives:\n\n`A Grammar of Motives` **398** · In-Game 84 · Phantasia 76 · Uncomfortable 69 · Aristotle 40 · VR Pedagogy 19 · Boredom Sec 17 · Dissertation 17 · FCM 16 · AMT 15 · H&R 15 · AES 13 · RDR2 Sec 12 · Wendt 12 · BT 11 · Uexkull 11 · **A Rhetoric of Motives 10** · BCAP 9 · Rickert 9.\n\nTwo entries bracket the range and the lesson is unambiguous: Grammar has 398 relations for 878 edges (free text); A Rhetoric of Motives has **10 relations for 420 edges, zero singletons**, because the closed set was declared in advance at `corpus/index/A Rhetoric of Motives (Burke 1950)/_synthesis/phase0-overview.md` before authoring began. Same pipeline family, same month, same author.\n\nCasing is also unnormalized: `depends_on`/`cites-as-support` coexist; `edge_domain` carries `Heidegger`/`Heideggerian`, `interpretive`/`interpretive-bridge`.\n\n### 2.4 Ontology dialects — **2 parser formats, 22 markdown files, 12 unread JSON twins**\n\n- **`header` format** (17 registered entries): `#### N. Name (qualifier)` headings with `- **field**:` bullets. Parsed by `parse_header_ontology`.\n- **`table` format** (2 registered entries): Aristotle (10 `*-ontology.md` files, reachable only because `analysis_subdir` is `None` at `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:76`) and BCAP.\n- **Filename dialects**: `book-level-ontology.md` (13) vs `cluster-ontology.md` (7, via the fallback at `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:1221-1223`) vs `*-ontology.md` glob (Aristotle only).\n- **12 entries ship a clean machine-readable ontology JSON that nothing reads**: Grammar, RM, AES, Phantasia, Boredom Sec, FCM, H&R, In-Game, RDR2 Sec, Uncomfortable, VR Pedagogy, Wendt. Three entries (Aristotelian Emotion, Phantasia, Boredom Secondary, VR Pedagogy) generated theirs with the compiler's own parser so they cannot drift — and the compiler still reads the markdown.\n- **Compiled nodes have no `id` field at all** (`sum(1 for n in ontologyNodes if 'id' in n) == 0`), so the entries' canonical slug IDs (`boredom-form-1`, `US-C-001`, `P-001`) can never be used to join edges to nodes at runtime. The runtime key is a display name.\n- **Section coverage**: only §3A is harvested. §3B trajectory, §3C tensions (30 authored in Aristotle alone), §3D contested nodes, §3E, §3F all reach nothing.\n\n### 2.5 Manifest shapes — **22 files across 21 entries; 6 entries have none**\n\n| Shape | Files | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Rich cluster manifest** — `sourceDir` + per-unit `sourceFile` + `ocrAudit` + `excluded[]` + `planCorrections` + `crossPipelineTargets` | Boredom Secondary, VR Pedagogy | best in corpus; all source paths resolve |\n| **Volume manifest with verified offset** — `volume.pdf_path`, `page_offset_formula`, 15-landmark `offset_verification`, machine-run `cite_check` | Grammar (`_synthesis/manifest.json`) | the template worth generalising |\n| **Hash-provenance manifest** — path + sha256 + bytes + lines + words per input, plus `sha256_prior_run`/deltas | Dissertation ×2 | only shape that supports drift detection |\n| **Segmentation manifest** — section records with `h_page`/`eng`/`pdf` ranges + `quality_checks` | BT, BCAP, Rickert, Uexkull | |\n| **Bare array, no schema/date/path** | Aristotle (`manifest.json`, 34-element list) | no source path at all |\n| **Media manifest** — absolute Windows-mount source dir | RDR2 Playthrough (`manifest.json:7`) | resolves locally, unresolvable on the Mac box |\n| **Thesis manifest** — repo-relative source PDF + declared 1:1 page-offset + 7 section ranges | Veri(dis)similitude (`manifest.json:11-35`) | 3 of its 5 declared counts are wrong |\n| **No manifest** | A Rhetoric of Motives, Phantasia Secondary, Game-Behavior, Presence Theory, Rhetoric of Interactivity, Social Presence | source path exists only in prose, or not at all |\n\n> Prior claim \"only ~10 manifests record source PDFs; 9 entries have NO machine-readable source path\" is **PARTIAL**. 21 of 27 entries have a manifest and most declare a resolvable source. The 6 with none are the correct target of that criticism.\n\n### 2.6 ID prefixes — 50 tokens matched, ~31 real unit-ID namespaces\n\nReal: `aes, amt, aud, bex, bor-sec, col, da, dfd, fcm, gm, hr, ig, ma, mem, meta, ped-sec, phx, phys, ptf, rdr, rhet, riv, rm, ss, svw, us, vle` plus Aristotle work keys and RDR2's temporal `pre/leadup/event/post`. That is **31, matching the prior claim**.\n\nCross-entry collisions that are real: `vle` appears in 5 entries; `da` means both *De Anima* (Aristotle) and *Debate Axis* (Boredom/VR Pedagogy); `ma` means *Movement of Animals* and *MA thesis*; `T-001` means both a tension and a temporal phase inside `corpus/index/In-Game (Calleja 2011)/_synthesis/`.\n\nUnenforced *within* entries: Grammar's unit records use `C-/P-/POS-/T-/TEN-/I-/INT-/X-/L-` plus 245 bare-slug IDs; Uncomfortable Situations carries four incompatible namespaces for one concept set (`US-C-001` in `_synthesis/book-level-ontology.json`, `C-US-01` in `_synthesis/concept-matrix.csv`, `C0##` in the `.mmd`, bare surnames in the edge CSVs) with **zero ID overlap and only 3 of 40 name matches**.\n\n### 2.7 Tension-edge schemas — **11 files, 4 yield zero silently**\n\nVerified by executing `_normalize_tension_edge` from the compiler against every file:\n\n| File | Yield | Schema |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Aristotle - Complete Works/tension-edges.json` | 12/12 | `node_a/node_b` + namespaced `CT-01..CT-12` |\n| `Heidegger and Rhetoric/_synthesis/tension-edges.json` | 12/12 | `tensions[]` with `node_a/node_b` |\n| `Von Uexkull/uex-analysis/tension-edges.json` | 10/10 | top-level list |\n| `Heidegger - Being and Time/bt-analysis/tension-edges.json` | 9/9 | no `id`, no `label`, no `units` — all 9 land with empty provenance |\n| `BCAP/bcap-analysis/tension-edges.json` | 7/7 | |\n| `FCM/_synthesis/tension-edges.json` | 7/7 | |\n| `Rickert/rickert-analysis/tension-edges.json` | 7/7 | |\n| **`A Grammar of Motives/_synthesis/tension-edges.json`** | **0/16** | `tension_id, label, description, source_unit_ids, pentad_terms_involved, centrality_tier, raw_unit_tension_count, provenance` |\n| **`In-Game/_synthesis/tension-edges.json`** | **0/12** | `tension_id, label, description, type, page_anchors, supporting_units, dissertation_implication` |\n| **`Uncomfortable Situations/_synthesis/tension-edges.json`** | **0/15** | `id, tension_name, pole_A, pole_B, evidence_pages_pdf, exemplified_in_units, resolved_by_gross_at` |\n| **`Wendt/_synthesis/tension-edges.json`** | **0/12** | `id, wendt_position, against, relation, unit, locus, note` |\n\n7 files × sum = 64 = the exact `tensionEdges` count in `compiled-index.json`. **55 authored tensions vanish with no warning.** Prior claim CONFIRMED exactly, including the four schema descriptions.\n\nEight further entries have **no tension file at all** despite authoring tensions in their unit records: Boredom Secondary (211), VR Pedagogy (98), Phantasia (46), RDR2 Secondary (56), AES (27), A Rhetoric of Motives (33 + 3 book-level), AMT (6), Dissertation. **704 tension records exist on disk; 64 reach runtime.**\n\n---\n\n## 3. Defects ranked\n\n### Tier 0 — systemic, corpus-wide, pipeline-level\n\n**S1. [CRITICAL] 24 of 27 entries are untracked in git and not gitignored.**\n`git ls-files corpus/index` returns 326 paths. Only `Boredom Experiment (VR Attention Study)` (9/9), `Boredom Secondary (Part III)` (189/189), `VR Pedagogy Secondary (Part III)` (127/127) and `compiled-index.json` are tracked. **1,433 files / ~30 MB — including every Burke, Heidegger, Aristotle and Dissertation artifact — exist only as working-tree bytes with no history and no recovery path.** `git check-ignore -v \"corpus/index/Aristotle - Complete Works/manifest.json\"` exits 1: nothing is deliberately excluded. This is the largest single risk to everything else in this report.\n\n**S2. [CRITICAL] The compiler reads 2.61% of the index and can never read more.**\n`scripts/compile-corpus-index.py` opens exactly 48 files (903,622 of 34,626,593 bytes). It has **no CSV reader** (`grep -c csv` = 0) and **no mermaid reader** (`grep -c mmd` = 0). `collect_ontology_nodes()` (:1195-1229) opens one ontology markdown per entry; `collect_cross_pipeline_hooks()` (:1233-1244) is hardcoded to `CORPUS_INDEX / \"Aristotle - Complete Works\"` with the comment \"Only Aristotle has cross-pipeline hook files\"; `collect_tension_edges()` (:1258-1275) opens one JSON per entry. Consequence: **9,702 edges, 3,597 claim records, 704 tensions, 1,623 mermaid arrows, 2,518 interlocutor records and every concordance in the corpus reach nothing.**\n\n**S3. [CRITICAL] 8 entries are unregistered; a further 13 are absent from the vector store; two entries are absent from both despite being the best-authored in the corpus.**\nUnregistered in `TEXT_DIRS` (`scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:35-133`, 19 keys): Aristotelian Emotion Secondary, Aristotelian Motion and Time, Aristotelian Phantasia Secondary, Dissertation, Game-Behavior Analysis Method, RDR2 Playthrough, RDR2 Secondary, Veri(dis)similitude. Note that `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:1219` names \"RDR2 Secondary, Phantasia Secondary\" in a comment explaining the `cluster-ontology.md` fallback — for two entries that are not `TEXT_DIRS` keys, so the fallback can never fire for them.\n`scripts/ingest/manifest.jsonl` covers only **14 of 27 entries**. **Boredom Secondary and VR Pedagogy — the two git-tracked, best-manifested entries — have zero ChromaDB rows.** A further **248 ingest rows failed with one identical bug**: `cannot access local variable 'bbox_chunks' where it is not associated with a value` (114 Aristotle, 42 BT, 36 Uexkull, 32 BCAP, 24 Rickert). That is a third reachability failure mode nobody had named.\n\n**S4. [HIGH] The header ontology parser corrupts node identity and pollutes the global term matcher.**\n`_parse_header_section` (`scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:689-693, 734-736`) splits `#### N. Name (qualifier)` at the parenthesis, truncates `name`, and files the qualifier into `greek`. `build_canonical_terms` (:1286) then harvests `greek`. Corpus-wide: **259 of 448 populated `greek` fields contain no Greek character** — 35 Uexkull, 34 BT, 30 Grammar, 28 H&R, 26 Boredom Sec, 24 FCM, 19 VR Pedagogy, 19 In-Game, 15 Uncomfortable, 8 RM, 5 Rhetoric of Interactivity, 4 VLE. Sample junk now inside `canonicalTerms`: `W25`, `global immersion`, `capstone prerequisite`, `gaze-based`, `spatial/physical`, `1976`, `HMD`, `control`, `technological`, `tiefe Langeweile / es ist einem langweilig`. 146 of the 1,722 canonical terms are short ASCII words including `action`, `debate`, `having`, `anyone`, `colour`, `breath`. The live consumer is a flat substring filter (`smart-retrieval-layer.ts:268`, `t.length >= 4 && queryLower.includes(t)`) granting a +0.10 rerank boost — so the bare word \"control\" can fire on \"controlled\".\n\n**S5. [HIGH] The parser runs away past node boundaries in 4 nodes and corrupts tier values in 8.**\nWorst case: `Preparatory Rhetoric` (Rickert) compiles with a `units` array of **973 tokens** and a `centralityTier` of `'peripheral --- ## 3b: global edge list | source | relation | edge domain | target | note | chapters | |-----…'` — the node swallowed the rest of the file. `Temporalität` (`corpus/index/Heidegger - Being and Time/bt-analysis/book-level-ontology.md:415-494`) has 586 unit tokens. Corpus-wide there are **1,056 distinct tokens in `ontologyNodes[].units`**, of which dozens are junk harvested from prose: `\"ambient`, `##`, `###`, `(Sorge)`, `(Vorlaufen)`, `(node/link`, `(aletheia).`, `(Part`, `\"who\"`. Eight nodes carry a `centralityTier` string longer than 20 characters.\n\n**S6. [HIGH] Name-keyed cross-text dedup silently destroys per-text definitions.**\n`deduplicate_ontology_nodes` (`scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:1311-1348`) merges by `node[\"name\"].lower()` across all 19 registered texts, keeps only the **longest** definition, unions `units` and joins `text` with `\"; \"`. **51 merged multi-text nodes** exist in `compiled-index.json`. Boredom Secondary's own readings of `Dasein`, `das Man`, `Pathos`, `Kairos` and `Enthymeme` are overwritten by Being-and-Time's, Gross's, Rickert's and Hyde's — while the merged node still lists Boredom Secondary in `text` and its units in `units`. 37 of Aristotle's 199 raw nodes are lost this way. The node *looks* attributed and carries someone else's gloss.\n\n**S7. [HIGH] The synthesis edge layer is lossy in four distinct, undocumented ways.**\n(a) key-collapse discarding `locus`/`note` (Boredom Sec, 21 rows); (b) comma-truncation destroying notes while restoring 5-column arity so no schema check can see it (VR Pedagogy, 12 notes + 2 loci, e.g. `_synthesis/global-edges.csv:625`, `:122`, `:414`); (c) ID-normalisation collapsing distinct page-level loci into one endpoint (Uncomfortable Situations, 2 rows lost + 12 self-loops at `_synthesis/global-edges.csv:133,313,349-368`); (d) namespace re-encoding (Aristotle, 212 of 245 per-source triples absent from the synthesis layer). Only Grammar records its delta.\n\n**S8. [HIGH] Zero quality gates that mean anything.**\nOnly 2 of 27 entries have a `quality-gates-report.md` (`Red Dead Redemption 2 Secondary (2019-2023)/_synthesis/`, `Wendt - Design for Dasein/_synthesis/`) and only 2 have a render validation (`Aristotelian Phantasia Secondary/_synthesis/render-validation.txt`, `Uncomfortable Situations/_synthesis/render-validation.txt`). Where machine-readable gate blocks exist inline they are unreliable: `corpus/index/Dissertation/_run-history/2026-05-13T1439/_per-section/DISS-01-A0/phase2-claims.json:1798` records a passing gate against an edge count off by 45; `.../DISS-05-A4/phase2-claims.json:259` reports 96 claims in a file whose own `total_claims` is 98; `corpus/index/A Grammar of Motives (Burke 1945)/Burke - Container and Thing Contained/gm-01-deep.json:339` certifies content-filter compliance its own `.md` twin falsifies in 31 places. Gate *values* are free-text strings mixing booleans and prose, so nothing can validate them mechanically.\n\n**S9. [MEDIUM] 46 ragged CSV rows corpus-wide caused by unquoted commas.**\nWendt 11, VR Pedagogy 10 (`Makransky & Petersen - Desktop VR SEM (2019)/ped-sec-11-…-edges.csv:22-27`), Boredom Sec 3 (`Elpidorou - The Good of Boredom (2018)/bor-sec-26-…-edges.csv:17,23,37`), Uncomfortable 2 (`Gross & Preston - Epilogue…/us-05-epilogue-edges.csv:7,20`), FCM 2, A Rhetoric of Motives 1 (`Burke - Pure Persuasion/edges.csv:24`), Dissertation 26. In VR Pedagogy 8 of the 10 carry `cites-cluster-author` — the join keys of the citation graph.\n\n**S10. [MEDIUM] 67 `.mmd` files / 1,623 arrow-lines across 15 entries reach nothing** — and several are *wrong*, not merely orphaned. `corpus/index/VR Pedagogy Secondary (Part III)/_synthesis/graph-citation-network.mmd:26` draws `p09 --> p06`, asserting a 2018 paper cites a 2021 model — an inversion the entry's own data explicitly forbids at `Makransky & Lilleholt - Emotional Value (2018)/ped-sec-09-…-edges.csv:22`, and which propagated into the prose at `_synthesis/citation-network.md:16-17`. 25 rendered `.svg` siblings are referenced by nothing.\n\n**S11. [MEDIUM] Stale cross-entry assertions that only a filesystem check can catch.**\nEight VR Pedagogy unit JSONs (e.g. `Cook et al. - TES Meta-Analysis (2011)/ped-sec-15-cook-tes-meta.json:68`) assert in a machine-readable field that the Boredom Experiment entry \"does not exist\" while three siblings say \"BUILT 2026-07-16\"; the same claim appears at `corpus/index/Boredom Secondary (Part III)/bridge-sources/anchor-pointers.md:31` and `_synthesis/manifest.json:178`. `corpus/index/VR Pedagogy Secondary (Part III)/_synthesis/citation-corrections-2026-07-16.md:52` states none of its corrections have been applied; all have. Two entries assert a compiler patch \"is required at Phase 5\" that shipped.\n\n**S12. [MEDIUM] Unicode-in-path breakage between entries.**\n`corpus/index/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/manifest.json:11` and `:15` — both machine-readable methodology pointers — spell the directory with ASCII `x` where the filesystem uses U+00D7 `×`. Both dangle. Same class: `corpus/index/Game-Behavior Analysis Method (Burke × Calleja)/CANONICAL-METHODOLOGY-v9.md:4,:14` uses an em dash where the target filename uses a hyphen.\n\n### Tier 1 — CRITICAL, entry-local\n\n- **`corpus/index/In-Game (Calleja 2011)/Calleja - From Immersion to Incorporation/ig-10-incorporation.json:155`** — the **only unparseable JSON of 494** (prior claim CONFIRMED exactly). Line 134 opens an object `{`, line 155 closes it `],`. One-character fix.\n- **`corpus/index/Aristotle - Complete Works/aristotle-phys-08.json:9`** and 32 siblings — 33 of 34 unit records carry `pdf_pages` from a superseded linear Bekker offset; errors reach 47 pages. `corpus/index/Aristotle - Complete Works/aristotle-bekker-index.json` — 101 of 188 loci deviate >2 pages, worst ~44. The correct per-work formulas exist three files away in `phase05-offset-validation.md`, verified against `pdfinfo`. mtime forensics: `aristotle-meta-05.json` (15:33:41) is the only corrected record; the bekker index was generated at 16:23:11 *with the discarded arithmetic*.\n- **`corpus/index/Heidegger - Being and Time/bt-analysis/book-level-ontology.md:33`** — the `Dasein` node's `units` field is authored as English prose, so BT's most central concept reaches runtime with zero valid unit references.\n- **`corpus/index/Uncomfortable Situations/_synthesis/concept-matrix.csv:2` vs `_synthesis/book-level-ontology.json`** — two incompatible concept registries in one directory, zero ID overlap, 3 of 40 name matches.\n\n### Tier 2 — HIGH, entry-local (selected; ~40 confirmed)\n\n- **Unresolved identifiers.** `corpus/index/A Grammar of Motives (Burke 1945)/_synthesis/global-edges.csv` — **876/876 rows carry `resolution_status: heuristic-pending-3A`**; only 13 of 963 distinct endpoints are real ontology IDs. `corpus/index/In-Game (Calleja 2011)/Calleja - From Immersion to Incorporation/ig-10-deep-edges.csv` — 847 of 1,472 per-unit endpoints (58%) are undeclared in their own unit's JSON; four units are at 100%. `corpus/index/Uncomfortable Situations/Gross - Introduction…/us-00-intro-edges.csv` — 490 of 746 (66%).\n- **Missing page anchors.** `corpus/index/A Rhetoric of Motives (Burke 1950)/Burke - Order and Ultimate Terms/rm-05-deep.json` — **143 of 160 concept records (89%) have no locus of any kind**. Grammar: 151 of 441 concepts, 53 of 101 positions, 35 of 70 tensions. Boredom Secondary: 246 of 2,258 sub-items.\n- **Refuted claims left live in the highest-value chunks.** `corpus/index/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/rdr2-element-matrix.md:57,:71,:89,:90` and `rdr2-vs-gg-differential.md:13,:21` still assert readings that `frame-read-verification.md:12,:14,:16` refuted a month earlier; `rdr2-tutorial-RODA.md:34` and `:131` contradict each other on the same verdict, and the wrong one is in the §8 summary paragraph. Identical pattern in `corpus/index/Veri(dis)similitude (Salvo MA)/`: `manifest.json:22`, `gg-frame-trace.md:72` (under a header reading \"RESOLVED\") and `gg-element-matrix.md:33` still certify as \"footage-confirmed\" the timestamps `gg-e6-dense-trace.md` overturned — and that correcting file's frame archive (`scratchpad/gg-e6-dense/`) no longer exists.\n- **Fabricated and altered quotations.** `corpus/index/VR Pedagogy Secondary (Part III)/Biocca Burgoon & Harms…/ped-sec-29-…md:7` presents \"sense of being in the place\" as verbatim with an FE page tag; the phrase does not occur in the Biocca PDF (the source has \"being in the virtual place\" and \"sense of the place\" separately). `corpus/index/Dissertation/_run-history/2026-05-13T1439/_synthesis/master-citation-report-parsed.json:176` silently rewrites White 1985's \"imagination (phantasia) is the process…\" to \"phantasia is the process…\" with no ellipsis. `:221` carries pdfium ligature loss (\"fgures\") in a verbatim marked `\"use\": \"in-text\"`.\n- **Destroyed primary evidence.** `corpus/index/Game-Behavior Analysis Method (Burke × Calleja)/VALIDATION-v4-barfight.md:4` and `v5:4` record that the transcript grounding all seven validation runs was cleared by a reboot; validations v4 onward are re-readings of v3's prose. `corpus/index/In-Game (Calleja 2011)/Calleja - Appendix…/ig-apx-appendix.json:10` anchors 995 line-ranges — the entry's finest addressing scheme — into `/tmp/calleja-fulltext.txt`, gone. 65 references in `corpus/index/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/frame-traces/RDR2 - Rape Scene -- raw-frame-logs/` point at a deleted scratchpad.\n- **The most valuable single directory in the corpus is orphaned.** `corpus/index/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/frame-traces/RDR2 - Rape Scene -- raw-frame-logs/` — 68 files, 69,080 words, 1,326 bullet observations, 1,040 distinct frame IDs — is referenced by no file in the entry; `phase0-overview.md` returns zero hits for it. A manifest-driven cleanup would delete 57% of the entry's markdown without noticing.\n- **Fabricated attribution in a searchable layer.** `corpus/index/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/transcripts/RDR2 - 1 - Opening Cinematic.txt:1-7` carries seven repetitions of a hallucinated third-party copyright credit naming a real-sounding person. 8 of 22 transcripts are 100% whisper hallucination; the manifest's caveat at `:19` names only 6 of the 8.\n- **Content-filter breaches self-certified as compliant.** `corpus/index/A Grammar of Motives (Burke 1945)/Burke - Symbolic Action in a Poem by Keats/gm-10-deep.md:21` — the mandatory \"no ≥25-word verbatim\" rule (`plans/grammar-of-motives-burke-1945-analysis.md:247,:392`) is breached in 31 places, longest 97 words; `corpus/index/A Rhetoric of Motives (Burke 1950)/Burke - Pure Persuasion/rm-07-deep.md:58` in 5 places, longest 81.\n- **Only the superseded version is retrievable.** `corpus/index/Game-Behavior Analysis Method (Burke × Calleja)/build_pdf.py:25-28` + `scripts/ingest/manifest.jsonl` — the 8 ingested files include the **v1 ancestor**; all seven canonical versions v2–v9 (48,809 words) are unreachable. Two other entries declare v9 as their methodology.\n\n### Appendix 3A — findings that did NOT survive verification\n\n| Finding | Entry | Why it failed |\n|---|---|---|\n| `concept-matrix.csv` joins to zero ontology nodes → \"four non-joinable namespaces\" [HIGH] | Heidegger - FCM | Tested against `book-level-ontology.json` slug IDs, which are themselves dead — compiled nodes have **no `id` key at all**. Joining on label recovers 12/45 exact, 24/45 to runtime nodes; the column axis joins 15/15 to units. Real residue: no stable key column, 21 rows unresolvable. **LOW.** |\n| `citation-gap-master.json` declares 207 gaps but ships 154 [HIGH] | Dissertation | Records-vs-gaps denominator error. Two entries are explicitly labelled batch records with rank ranges (`:2211`, `:2224`); expanding them gives exactly 207 over a contiguous 1..207 space with no gaps or duplicates, and the strategy is documented in `synthesis_notes.compilation_strategy`. Real residue: one off-by-one on DISS-02. **LOW.** |\n| `manifest.json` declares 22 synthesis files, 24 exist [HIGH] | RDR2 Secondary | The metric is named \"Synthesis **deliverables** (phantasia-cluster parity)\". The phantasia `_synthesis` contains exactly 22 files and no manifest/gate report. 22 is correct; 24 would have been the error. **Not a defect.** |\n| `vle-05` source PDF does not exist anywhere [CRITICAL] | Virtual Learning Environments | The `find` was scoped to this repo. The PDF is at the exact declared relative path under the archon corpus root. All six §7 drafting loci verified byte-exact against it. Real residue: the entry mixes two corpus roots (`vle-04:3` vs `vle-05:3`), and `vle-05:3` declares \"(15 PDF pp.)\" for a 14-page document. **LOW.** |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Cross-entry patterns\n\n**Systemic — a property of the pipeline, not of any author:**\n\n1. **Runtime blindness.** Every entry authors 20–100× more structure than the compiler can see. This is a property of `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py`, and no amount of authoring care changes it. It is the root cause of ~40% of all filed defects.\n2. **Dual serialization with no declared authority.** 15 entries maintain both a per-source and a synthesis edge layer. **Not one** declares which wins in a machine-readable field. Only Grammar documents its delta. Four entries disagree for four different reasons.\n3. **Correction can never reach the artifact it corrects, because rows have no IDs.** This is the single most damaging recurring pattern and it is invariant across media. RDR2 Playthrough (prose beat rows), Veri(dis)similitude (prose matrix rows), VR Pedagogy (`citation-corrections-2026-07-16.md`), Aristotle (the offset fix applied to prose and not to JSON), Boredom Secondary (`contested-readings.md` CR-12a/b/c cited but never defined). In every case the correction was written as a *new document* because there was no addressable row to edit. Add IDs without adding a `supersedes` edge and this will recur.\n4. **Summary blocks contradict the data in the same file.** In-Game: `ig-bibliography-extracted.json:24,267,269,271` gives four incompatible counts; `ig-interlocutor-map.json:815-822` says 66 for a 73-element array; `ig-terminology-appendix.json:154` says 132 for 141. Uncomfortable: `book-level-ontology.json:17-21`. Boredom Secondary: `cluster-ontology.md:135` (TERM 24 vs 25, DEBATE-AXIS 12 vs 8, METHOD omitted — the two errors cancel so any total-only check passes). Grammar: 6 of 14 units mis-report their own edge count. A Rhetoric of Motives: 6 of 8.\n5. **Phase-ordering artifacts frozen into data.** Debate-axis IDs (`DA-NN`) are a Phase-3B deliverable; edges are Phase-2. Result: **zero of 260 `shifts-debate-axis` rows corpus-wide begin with an ID token** — Boredom 56 rows/46 spellings, VR Pedagogy 40/21, RDR2 22/22, Phantasia 11/1, AES 1/1. The vocabulary exists; it simply post-dates its consumers.\n6. **`/tmp` as an evidence store.** In-Game (6 paths), Uncomfortable (2), Game-Behavior (1, destroyed), RDR2 Playthrough (65 references), Veri(dis)similitude (1). Every one is gone. The pattern correlates with the finest-grained evidence in each entry.\n7. **German written into a field named `greek`** (259 of 448 populated values), and node names truncated at parentheses. Both are parser-contract mismatches nobody could see from inside an entry.\n\n**One-off:**\n- The Aristotle offset abandonment (a single interrupted repair, reconstructible from mtimes).\n- `ig-10-incorporation.json:155` (one character).\n- The RDR2 U+00D7 path (one character, two lines).\n- Grammar's 398-value relation vocabulary — one entry, one decision not to declare a closed set.\n\n**Outliers, and why:**\n- **Dissertation** — indexes the user's *own* prose, not a source. Has the finest granularity in the corpus (1 claim per 58 words) and the best provenance apparatus (sha256+bytes+lines+words per input, with prior-run deltas), and is registered nowhere. Its 273 `.md` are in ChromaDB and its 69 `.json` are not — the exact inversion of what should be true.\n- **Game-Behavior Analysis Method** — not an index at all. It is the *instrument*. 11 structured records for 82,134 words. Its correct role in a redesign is as the controlled vocabulary (R1–R7, A0–A4, the 6×6 Burke×Calleja grid), not as an entry.\n- **A Rhetoric of Motives** — the only entry that declared a closed relation vocabulary and a binary provenance rule *before* authoring, and honoured both. 420 edges, 10 relations, 0 singletons, 0 empty cells, 0 duplicate triples. It ships half the apparatus of its sibling Grammar and is structurally healthier for it.\n- **Aristotelian Motion and Time Secondary** — 5 files, 1 unit. An abandoned stub with a manifest.\n- **The six Part III \"lite\" entries** (Boredom Experiment, Presence Theory, Rhetoric of Interactivity, Social Presence, VLE, plus Veri(dis)similitude) — md-only, 7–10 files, no unit JSON, no edges. Five are registered and contribute 52 runtime nodes on 25,203 words. They are the cheapest nodes-per-hour in the corpus and the least able to support anything below concept level.\n\n---\n\n## 5. What is genuinely excellent\n\nThese are the artifacts that ~40 hours per entry actually bought. A redesign must carry them forward **verbatim**; they are the expensive part and the hardest to reproduce.\n\n**Provenance discipline — the single most valuable invention in the corpus.**\nThe three-way tag `FE` (the source's own published claim) / `FAITHFUL-<author>` (close paraphrase of a specific passage) / `P-anticipatory-application` (the project's own interpretive link, never the source's). Corpus-wide: **1,107 FE tags, 1,265 FAITHFUL tags, 922 anticipatory-application tags**. The rule is written down at `corpus/index/Boredom Secondary (Part III)/bridge-sources/anchor-pointers.md:157-161`. The same discipline appears as a mandatory binary field in `corpus/index/A Rhetoric of Motives (Burke 1950)/_synthesis/global-edges.csv` — all 420 edges carry `provenance ∈ {burke-direct 325, anticipatory-projection 95}`, zero blanks — and as `provenance` on all 736 rows of In-Game's edge layer. This is what makes a claim-level index safe to build. Nothing else in the corpus is as reusable.\n\n**Verified page-offset formulas with landmark tables.**\n`corpus/index/A Grammar of Motives (Burke 1945)/_synthesis/manifest.json` — `page_offset_formula: \"PDF page = book page + 21\"` with a **15-landmark verification table naming the exact first line extracted at each landmark**, plus a machine-run `cite_check` (PyMuPDF regex over all 551 pages: Aristotle 112 hits/63 pages, Spinoza 114/53, Korzybski 36/19, Santayana 42/21) and an `ocr_audit_summary` naming the exact artifacts to expect (`explicidy`, `sufficiendy`, `elementaiism`). `corpus/index/Aristotle - Complete Works/phase05-offset-validation.md` — per-work compression ratios (1.250–2.000 PDF pp. per Bekker page) from 133 OCR-detected margin landmarks across three zones per work, with an error column; its stated page counts match `pdfinfo` exactly. `corpus/index/Uncomfortable Situations/_synthesis/manifest.json:29` — one offset rule, 8 landmarks, restated in all four loci concordances, and **zero fulltext line-anchors anywhere in the entry**, which is why its evidence survived the loss of its `/tmp` extracts while In-Game's did not.\n\n**Refusal to fabricate, recorded as data.**\n`corpus/index/Boredom Secondary (Part III)/_synthesis/manifest.json:32` — the bor-sec-18 agent refused to build a unit under a false attribution when the on-disk \"Standish (2015)\" PDF proved to be Mertel (2020), verified three ways (pdfinfo Title, Subject line, CreationDate, full-text diff). `:35-45` records that an *earlier* correction of bor-sec-44 was itself wrong and why. `:47-60` refuses to fabricate bridges for three units whose sources genuinely do not engage FCM, and documents the plan's own internal contradiction rather than picking a side. `corpus/index/VR Pedagogy Secondary (Part III)/_synthesis/manifest.json` planCorrections — a mislabeled PDF caught by `pdfinfo` before any content was built on it.\n\n**Falsification passes that overturned the project's own hypotheses.**\n`corpus/index/In-Game (Calleja 2011)/_synthesis/manifest.json` `cite_check.gibson` — \"CRITICAL FINDING — GIBSON ABSENT… The Gibson-as-implicit-Uexküll-bridge hypothesis (plan v3 §5 Phase 0) is FALSIFIED\", with the 11 generic hits counted. `corpus/index/VR Pedagogy Secondary (Part III)/_synthesis/cluster-ontology.md` §1,§5 — the CMC-to-VR social-presence bridge the plan anticipated \"mostly does not exist in the literature itself\", verified by full-text checks. `corpus/index/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/frame-read-verification.md` — 10 named claims with CONFIRMED / REFUTED / UNCLEAR / RESOLVED verdicts, three of them against the prior reading. `corpus/index/Veri(dis)similitude (Salvo MA)/manifest.json:55-62` `cite_check_RODA_pillars` — per-pillar ABSENT/PARTIAL/PROTO/PRESENT coverage audit with the gap assigned to Part I.\n\n**Claim-shaped record types that already work.**\n`corpus/index/Uncomfortable Situations/Gross - Radcliffe…/us-03-radcliffe.json` `positions[]` = `{position_id, claimant, claim, support (list of page loci), contested_by}` — claimant, proposition, evidence and opposition in one record. `corpus/index/A Rhetoric of Motives (Burke 1950)/Burke - Order and Ultimate Terms/rm-05-deep.json` `positions[0]` = `{id:'P1', claim:'…', book_page:183, provenance:'burke-direct'}` — 53 records, 100% with an `id`, 47/53 page-anchored, 100% provenance-tagged. `corpus/index/Veri(dis)similitude (Salvo MA)/vds-claims-moves.md` — **157 uniquely-ID'd, page-anchored claims** with a closed disposition vocabulary (keep-verbatim / re-ground / enrich / supersede / drop) and a closed RODA-anchor enum, verified zero duplicate IDs. `corpus/index/Dissertation/_run-history/2026-05-13T1439/_per-section/*/phase2-claims.json` — 982 line-anchored claims, 8-level support tier (T1 277 / T2 78 / T3 477 / T4 41 / T5 71 / T6 12 / T7 22 / T8 4), 76% in a supports/supported_by DAG, each with a machine-readable `remediation` object naming routing candidates and an effort estimate.\n\n**Sub-page evidence layers.**\n`corpus/index/Uncomfortable Situations/_synthesis/` four loci concordances (emotion 60, literary 50, neuroscience 35, rhetoric 31 = **176 phrase-level records**, each with source citation, evidential phrase, commentary page and tier). `corpus/index/Aristotle - Complete Works/aristotle-bekker-index.json` — 188 loci each bound to a description, concept list and unit_id, 187/188 correctly inside their unit's declared range (only the `pdf_page` column is wrong). `corpus/index/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/frame-traces/RDR2 - Rape Scene -- raw-frame-logs/` — 1,040 frame IDs with an explicit `t = 149 + (n-1)/24` mapping.\n\n**Perfect internal consistency where it was actually enforced.**\n`corpus/index/A Grammar of Motives (Burke 1945)/_synthesis/concept-matrix.csv` — all 56 concept IDs match `book-level-ontology.json` exactly, and for all 56 rows the marked-cell count equals both the declared total and the ontology's unit set. Zero drift. `corpus/index/VR Pedagogy Secondary (Part III)/_synthesis/concept-matrix.csv` — bit-exact against the ontology on all 34 columns; `bridge-sources/anchor-pointers.md` validates 100% against the per-unit CSVs on all 34 rows. `corpus/index/Boredom Secondary (Part III)` — 55/55 units, 165/165 expected files, 0 JSON failures, 0 dangling `bor-sec-*` references in any of 189 files.\n\n**Operational instruments, not summaries.**\n`corpus/index/In-Game (Calleja 2011)/_synthesis/ig-pim-operationalization-manual.md` (10,078 words: six dimension entries, incorporation rubric, WoW worked example, question battery, three-layer augmentation). `corpus/index/A Rhetoric of Motives (Burke 1950)/_synthesis/rm-identification-consubstantiation-manual.md` — states the homology then enumerates five explicit divergences and labels every projective claim inline. `corpus/index/Uncomfortable Situations/_synthesis/contested-nodes.md` — 10 concepts, each separating \"surface convergence\" from \"underlying tension\", both cited. `corpus/index/A Grammar of Motives (Burke 1945)/_synthesis/contested-nodes.md` — five-part taxonomy of contestation types with cross-volume frequency and enumerated senses.\n\n**Executable specs written before the work.**\n`corpus/index/A Rhetoric of Motives (Burke 1950)/_synthesis/phase0-overview.md` declares the required JSON field schema with cardinality minimums (concepts ≥15, positions ≥4, tensions ≥2), the required `.md` section list, the exact `pdftotext` command, a closed 10-value relation set and a content filter. I tested all 8 units: **every cardinality gate passes** (concepts 17–26, positions 5–9, tensions 3–6). The spec was written first and obeyed. This is the cheapest quality mechanism in the corpus and it cost one file.\n\n---\n\n## 6. The granularity verdict\n\n### 6.1 Finest unit encoded today, entry by entry\n\n| Granularity | Entries | Finest addressable object |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Clause-adjacent (sub-page, already)** | RDR2 Playthrough | frame ID at 24 fps (`e_0001`, `l_0385`), 1,040 distinct, with `t = 149+(n-1)/24` |\n| | In-Game | 995 line-range anchors into a **deleted** fulltext |\n| | Uncomfortable Situations | 176 concordance loci carrying a *phrase* + its rhetorical figure + dual page anchors |\n| | Aristotle | 2,323 distinct Bekker line-loci (`429a1–2`) in prose — the canonical clause address system for the author |\n| **Claim (proposition + locus)** | Dissertation | 982 line-anchored claim records, 1 per 58 source words |\n| | Veri(dis)similitude | 157 ID'd, page-anchored, dispositioned claims, 1 per 99 words |\n| | Boredom Secondary | 463 `readings` (`claim`/`type`/`stance`/`locus`/`tag`) |\n| | VR Pedagogy | 233 `readings`, same shape |\n| | Uncomfortable / RM / Grammar / In-Game | 73 / 53 / 113 / 89 `positions` |\n| | FCM / Wendt | 182 / 139 `claims` |\n| **Sub-chapter section** | Grammar (139 `outline`), RM (84), In-Game (85), Phantasia (181), BT (83 §-records), BCAP, Rickert, Uexkull | section with page range |\n| **Chapter / article** | AES, AMT, RDR2 Secondary, H&R, Aristotle records | the unit itself |\n| **Book / concept only** | Presence Theory, Social Presence, Rhetoric of Interactivity, VLE, Boredom Experiment, Game-Behavior | a concept node; no unit records at all |\n\n**At runtime, for every one of the 27 entries, the finest addressable object is a concept name.** 701 of them. No claim, no edge, no locus, no quotation has any runtime existence whatsoever.\n\n### 6.2 Claim-level material that already exists — quantified\n\n**Structured, on disk, today:**\n\n| Record type | Count | Distinct |\n|---|---|---|\n| `readings` | 929 | 929 |\n| `positions` | 383 | 383 |\n| `claims` | 2,285 | 1,303 (Dissertation's 1,964 is 982 × 2 runs) |\n| **Claim-shaped total** | | **2,615** |\n| `tensions` (claim-vs-claim pairs) | 704 | 704 |\n| `sections` (sub-chapter) | 1,186 | |\n| `outline` (sub-chapter) | 590 | |\n| `loci` / `aristotle_loci` (phrase-level) | 872 | |\n| `concepts` | 3,044 | |\n| `interlocutors` | 2,518 | |\n| `constructs` / `measures` / `game_elements` / `conditions` | 1,038 | |\n\n**Unstructured, in prose, today** — 1,899,804 words of markdown across 865 files:\n\n| Signal | Corpus total | Densest entries |\n|---|---|---|\n| Quoted spans ≥25 chars | **25,825** | Aristotle 2,418 · Boredom Sec 2,547 · BCAP 2,362 · Dissertation 2,378 · FCM 2,088 · BT 1,733 · RDR2 Playthrough 1,394 |\n| Page-locus mentions (`p.NN`/`pp.NN`) | **16,256** | Boredom Sec 2,930 · FCM 2,451 · H&R 1,316 · VR Ped 1,281 · BCAP 1,248 · Uexkull 1,085 · Aristotle 1,025 · Wendt 958 |\n| Bekker/line loci (`429a1`) | **10,094** | Aristotle 6,283 · Dissertation 1,733 · Phantasia 1,050 · H&R 338 · AES 256 |\n| FE / FAITHFUL / anticipatory tags | **3,294** | Boredom Sec 1,681 · VR Ped 1,138 |\n\nThe ratio that matters: **VR Pedagogy holds 233 structured `readings` and ~1,277 provenance-tagged, page-anchored assertions in its prose — 5.5×.** Boredom Secondary holds 463 structured and ~1,681 tagged. If that ratio holds corpus-wide, roughly **14,000 claim-level assertions are already written and merely unparsed**, against 2,615 structured. **The claim-level programme is predominantly a parsing job, not an authoring job.** That should change its cost estimate by an order of magnitude.\n\n### 6.3 Mechanical decomposition vs re-authoring\n\n**Mechanically decomposable now (parse + normalize, no re-reading):**\n- **Dissertation** — already there; needs schema unification across 6 dialects and promotion of free-text `ARISTOTLE-LOCUS:`/`HEIDEGGER-LOCUS:` edge targets to IDs.\n- **Veri(dis)similitude** — 5 markdown tables, 4 of them single-dialect, 262 ID'd rows. Serialize and register.\n- **Boredom Secondary, VR Pedagogy** — 696 `readings` need one normalization pass to `{id: '<prefix>-NN-Rmm', claim, locus, stance∈enum, tag∈enum}`; both entries' prose then yields ~2,900 more.\n- **A Rhetoric of Motives, Uncomfortable Situations** — 126 well-formed `positions` need only IDs and a compiler slot. Uncomfortable's 176 concordance loci are already phrase-level.\n- **Aristotle** — 973 Bekker-anchored bullets and 129 already-ID'd `UNIT-NN-Pn` propositions; blocked only because 34 analyses use 30+ heading conventions. Standardizing the template retroactively is the single highest-leverage move in the corpus.\n- **RDR2 Playthrough** — 1,326 observations and 284 beat rows; needs IDs + an evidence-grade enum, not new observation.\n\n**Needs partial re-authoring:**\n- **Grammar, In-Game** — the claim records exist (113 + 89 positions) but 7 positions are bare strings, 40 lack prefixed IDs, 53 lack a page. In-Game additionally needs `/tmp/calleja-fulltext.txt` regenerated under a recorded deterministic command before its 995 line-anchors mean anything.\n- **BT, BCAP, Rickert, Uexkull, H&R** — 108 BT claim records exist only as markdown table cells inside prose (`corpus/index/Heidegger - Being and Time/bt-analysis/phase2-bt-d1-u2.md:85-96`), with 84 explicit claim-to-tension back-references. Extractable, but per-entry parsers.\n- **FCM, Wendt, RDR2 Secondary, Phantasia, AES** — claim slots exist and are sparsely populated.\n\n**Needs full re-authoring:**\n- The six md-only Part III lite entries (Presence Theory, Social Presence, Rhetoric of Interactivity, VLE, Boredom Experiment) — 25,203 words total, 15 units, no unit records at all. Cheap to redo at claim level precisely because they are small.\n- **Game-Behavior Analysis Method** — cannot be decomposed to claim level because it indexes no document. It should become the schema source.\n\n**Structurally incapable regardless of effort, without a policy change:** the *clause text itself* is deliberately absent from three entries. `corpus/index/In-Game (Calleja 2011)/Calleja - From Immersion to Incorporation/ig-10-deep.json:434-441` and `corpus/index/Uncomfortable Situations/Gross - Radcliffe…/us-03-radcliffe.json:110,:234` record that every ≥25-word block was paraphrased under a content filter. **A clause-level index needs the clause.** That filter must be revisited or those entries can never reach the target.\n\n### 6.4 The multiplier — arithmetic from observed data\n\n**Source corpus actually indexed.** The five primary source directories hold **18,557 PDF pages across 210 documents** (`rhetorical_ontology` 10,296 / 63 · `new_media` 3,108 / 43 · `boredom` 3,572 / 50 · `metaphysics` 943 / 19 · `pedagogy` 638 / 35). The index covers roughly 130 of those documents: ~12 monographs (Aristotle 553 verified, Grammar 551 verified, BT ~490, RM 356, FCM ~370, BCAP ~340, Rickert ~300, H&R ~250, Uncomfortable ~230, Uexkull ~230, In-Game ~200, Wendt ~200 ≈ **4,070 pp.**) plus ~118 articles (Boredom 50, VR Pedagogy 34, RDR2 Sec 12, Phantasia 8, AES 5, AMT 1, Part III lite 15, at ~20 pp. avg ≈ **2,530 pp.**). **≈ 6,600 indexed source pages ≈ 2.64 M source words** at ~400 words/page.\n\n**Claims.** Two independent estimators:\n- *Observed density.* Dissertation achieved 982 claims over 56,713 words = **1 claim / 58 words**. Veri(dis)similitude: 157 / 15,481 = 1 / 99. Applying 1/58–1/99 to 2.64 M words → **26,700 – 45,500 claims.**\n- *Per-page.* 3–5 substantive propositions per page × 6,600 pages → **20,000 – 33,000 claims.**\n\nConverging range: **≈ 25,000 – 40,000 claims.**\n\n**Clauses.** 2.64 M source words ÷ 12–18 words per clause → **147,000 – 220,000 clauses.** Cross-check from Aristotle alone: 2,323 distinct Bekker line-loci are already recorded in prose for 553 pages = 4.2 clause-addresses per page; extrapolated at that (very conservative, since it counts only *cited* lines) → 27,700; the true clause count for Aristotle's 553 pages at ~23 clauses/page is ~12,700 for that entry alone.\n\n**Multipliers against today:**\n\n| Layer | Today | Complete | Multiplier |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Addressable units | 362 | 362 | 1× |\n| Claim records | 2,615 (of which 0 at runtime) | 25,000 – 40,000 | **10× – 15×** on structure; **∞** on runtime |\n| Clause records | 0 | 147,000 – 220,000 | **new layer** |\n| Edges | 9,702 unit-to-string | claim-to-claim at ~2–3 per claim | **50,000 – 120,000** |\n| Runtime records | 701 nodes + 72 hooks + 64 tensions = 837 | ≥ 200,000 | **≈ 240×** |\n\nTwo thirds of the claim work is already *written*: ~14,000 tagged prose assertions + 2,615 structured records ≈ 16,600 of a 25,000–40,000 target, i.e. **40–66% of the claim layer already exists as text**. What does not exist at all is the clause layer and any addressing scheme below the page.\n\n### 6.5 Foundation or obstacle — the plain answer\n\n**The scholarship is a foundation. The format is an obstacle. The registration path is a wall.**\n\nThree specific structural properties make the current format incapable of the goal, and none of them is fixable by authoring more entries the same way:\n\n1. **The finest locator in the entire corpus is a page number.** Nothing on disk carries a sentence offset, a character span, or a bbox. Where sub-page anchors were attempted (In-Game's 995 line-ranges), they pointed into a `/tmp` file that no longer exists. Aristotle's Bekker line numbers are the one genuine exception, and they live in markdown bullets under 30 different heading conventions.\n2. **The edge model cannot express a claim-to-claim relation.** Every one of the 9,702 edges is keyed on `(source, relation, target)` where both endpoints are unit IDs or free-text strings, with `locus` as an unindexed note column. At claim granularity, endpoint collisions become the norm — and `corpus/index/Boredom Secondary (Part III)/_synthesis/global-edges.csv` already demonstrates what happens: a dedup key of `(s,r,t)` destroyed the `locus` and `note` of 21 rows, 12 of them the passage-level Heidegger bridges that are the entry's most valuable data. **The synthesis step deletes exactly the evidence the goal requires**, and it will delete more of it the deeper the index goes.\n3. **There is no runtime slot for a claim, a tension, an edge, a quotation or a locus.** `compiled-index.json` has four arrays and none of them is any of those. Adding 40,000 claims to the current format produces 40,000 records that reach nothing, at the current 2.61% read surface.\n\nThe corrective is not a rebuild. It is: keep every reading, position, claim, locus, provenance tag, correction ledger, offset table and cite-check verbatim; replace the *serialization* (one unit-JSON schema, one edge dialect, one ID namespace, one locus vocabulary extending to character spans); replace the *edge model* (claim-to-claim endpoints, five-column identity, no lossy dedup); and replace the *registration path* (read the JSON that 12 entries already ship, not one markdown section).\n\n---\n\n## 7. The ten things that must be true before any entry is authored again\n\n**1. Every file is in git before the first byte of analysis is written.**\n*Evidence:* 24 of 27 entries — 1,433 files, ~30 MB, including all of Aristotle, Burke, Heidegger and Dissertation — are untracked and not gitignored (`git ls-files corpus/index` returns 326 paths). There is no history, no diff, no recovery, and no way to tell an authored correction from an accidental overwrite. Every other item on this list is worthless if the bytes can vanish.\n\n**2. The registration path is proven end-to-end before authoring, with a JSON reader.**\n*Evidence:* the compiler opens 48 of 1,759 files (2.61% of bytes), has zero CSV and zero mermaid support, and hardcodes cross-pipeline hooks to one directory (`scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:1239`). 12 entries ship a clean ontology JSON that nothing reads while the markdown twin is parsed and corrupts 259 `greek` fields and 4 node boundaries. An entry that cannot demonstrate a record round-tripping to `compiled-index.json` on day one will not have one on day 400.\n\n**3. Every addressable object has a globally-unique, prefixed, immutable ID — including claims, edges, tensions and quotations.**\n*Evidence:* reading IDs `C1..C19` collide across 6 Boredom Secondary units; Uncomfortable Situations carries four incompatible namespaces for one concept set with zero overlap; compiled nodes have **no `id` field at all**; and the entire one-directional-correction failure (RDR2, Veri(dis), Aristotle, VR Pedagogy) traces to rows that cannot be addressed, so corrections could only be written as new documents that the corrected files never reference.\n\n**4. A `supersedes` / `superseded_by` edge exists and is mandatory for any correction.**\n*Evidence:* `corpus/index/Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)/frame-read-verification.md:23,:29` claims to correct two beat-maps; **zero of 22 beat-maps contain the string \"frame-read-verification\"**. Five refuted claims sit live in the entry's highest-retrieval chunks including a §8 summary paragraph. `corpus/index/Veri(dis)similitude (Salvo MA)/gg-e7-dense-trace.md:3` declares it supersedes `gg-frame-trace.md`; that file contains zero hits for \"dense\", and three files still certify the refuted reading as \"confirmed\".\n\n**5. Controlled vocabularies are declared in a machine-readable spec BEFORE authoring, and validated after.**\n*Evidence:* `corpus/index/A Rhetoric of Motives (Burke 1950)/_synthesis/phase0-overview.md` declared 10 relations and a binary provenance rule in advance — result: 420 edges, 10 relations, zero singletons, zero empty cells. Grammar did not — result: **398 relations for 878 edges**. Same pipeline family, same month. Corpus-wide: 633 relations, 162 `stance` values over 463 readings, 46 free-text spellings for 11 debate axes, and zero of 260 `shifts-debate-axis` rows using an axis ID.\n\n**6. One unit-record schema and one edge dialect, enforced by a validator that runs on commit.**\n*Evidence:* **146 distinct unit-JSON key signatures** and **44 edge-CSV header dialects** for 27 entries. `readings` alone takes 8 incompatible sub-shapes inside one entry; three interchangeable locus keys; five column-count variants inside Grammar. 46 ragged rows exist because no validator ever ran, and 12 of them were \"repaired\" by truncation into the synthesis layer where they now parse cleanly and carry wrong values.\n\n**7. No derived layer may be lossy, and every derived file must record its generator command and its source-layer hash.**\n*Evidence:* four dual-layer entries disagree for four different reasons and only one documents its delta. Boredom Secondary's dedup destroyed `locus`+`note` on 21 rows; VR Pedagogy's \"dedup\" removed 2 rows that were not duplicates and truncated 12 notes; Uncomfortable's ID merge created 12 self-loops; FCM's synthesis layer is a *superset* nobody flagged. Grammar's `_synthesis/canonical-id-resolution-report.md:33-37` is the only honest record and should be the template.\n\n**8. Every locus resolves to a character span in an archived, hash-verified extraction — never to `/tmp` and never to a page alone.**\n*Evidence:* In-Game's 995 line-anchors, Uncomfortable's two derived appendices, Game-Behavior's validation transcript, RDR2's 65 frame-log references and Veri(dis)'s 2 fps frame archive all point into deleted scratch space. Meanwhile Uncomfortable Situations survived intact **because it used only page anchors under one declared offset rule** — proof that durable addressing is a choice. Also: `corpus/index/Aristotle - Complete Works/aristotle-bekker-index.json` has 101 of 188 loci wrong by >2 pages because a superseded arithmetic was never re-run, while the correct formula sat three files away in `phase05-offset-validation.md`.\n\n**9. Every quotation is a first-class object with its own page, its own span, and a verified flag — one tag may not cover four quotations.**\n*Evidence:* 25,825 quoted spans of ≥25 characters exist across the index; almost none is individually addressable. `corpus/index/VR Pedagogy Secondary (Part III)/Biocca…/ped-sec-29-…md:7` presents a conflated phrase as verbatim with an FE tag, and it survived because one paragraph-terminal `(FAITHFUL-X, p.461-465)` tag covered four distinct quotations. `corpus/index/Dissertation/…/master-citation-report-parsed.json:176` silently drops a parenthetical from a White 1985 verbatim; `:221` ships pdfium ligature loss (\"fgures\") in a quotation marked for in-text use. Three entries deliberately deleted the clause text under a content filter and can never support clause-level indexing until that is reversed.\n\n**10. A machine-readable gate report is a deliverable, and every declared count is computed, never typed.**\n*Evidence:* 2 of 27 entries have a gate report; 2 have a render validation. Where inline gates exist they pass on wrong numbers (`DISS-01-A0/phase2-claims.json:1798`, off by 45; `gm-01-deep.json:339`, certifying compliance its own twin breaches 31 times). Hand-typed summary blocks are wrong in at least 9 entries — In-Game's bibliography gives four incompatible counts of itself; Boredom Secondary's `cluster-ontology.md:135` gets two of five node-type figures wrong in a way that cancels so any total-only check passes; Veri(dis)similitude has 3 of 5 manifest counts wrong. Note also what a gate must *not* be: `RDR2 Secondary`'s `synthesis_files: 22` is correct and certifies nothing — a cluster could pass it with 22 empty files. Gates must measure content, not cardinality."
  },
